    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McGill-College-2001/Invigilators_JR0000080083": {
      "title": "Invigilators",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Job Description Helps administer the delivery of the exams and documentation at the Montreal General Hospital. Ensures that students comply with regulations with respect to exams. Alerts professor when students have a question or a concern, if arises. At the end of the examination period, collects all exam materials and ensures nothing is left behind in the examination room(s). Responsible for reporting back to the administrator/program director and ensure delivery of the exams.    EDUCATION/EXPERIENCE REQUIRED Understanding and commitment to maintaining appropriate standards of confidentiality and security of materials. Adhering to McGill University policies and procedures. Ability to work independently. Dependability, reliability, punctuality. Please note that all exams are scheduled in Room 102 and Room 222 1. DENT 222 (Radiology) – Mon, Oct 5th, (1-3 PM) 2. DENT 248 (Periodontics) – Tue, Oct 13th, (9-11 AM) 3. DENT 322 (Radiology) – Wed, Oct 21st, (1-3 PM) 4. DENT 241 (Cariology) – Tue, Nov 3rd, (10-12 PM) 5. DENT 319 (Pharmacology) – Mon, Nov 30th, (9-11 AM) 6.  DENT 320 (Restorative) – Mon, Dec 7th (9-11:30 AM) 7. DENT 437 (CDM) – Mon Dec 7th (1-4 PM) 8. DENT 241 (Cariology) – Mon, Dec 7th, (1-3 PM) – Room 222 9. DENT 248 (Perio) – Tue, Dec 8th (9-12 PM) 10. DENT 111 (Intro to Dent) – Tue, Dec 8th (1-4 PM) 11. DENT 323 (OMFS) – Wed, Dec 9th (9-12 PM) 12. DENT 418 (Perio) – Wed, Dec 9th (1-4 PM) 13. DENT 242 (Operative) – Thu, Dec 10th (9-12 PM) 14. DENT 315 (Ortho) – Fri, Dec 11th (9-12 PM) 15. DENT 409 (Adv Restorative) – Fri, Dec 11th (1-4 PM) 16. DENT 318 (Perio) – Mon, Dec 14th (1-4 PM) 17. DENT 240 (Dental Ana & Occl) – Wed, Dec 16th, (9-12 PM) 18. DENT 415 (Ortho) – Wed, Dec 16th (1-4 PM) 19. DENT 322 (Radiology) – Thu, Dec 17th (9-12 PM) 20. DENT 222 (Intro to Radiology) – Thu, Dec 17th (1-4 PM) 21. DENT 343 (Endo) – Fri, Dec 18th (1-4 PM) – Room 222 22. DENT 411 (Endo) – Fri, Dec 18th (1-4 PM) 23. DENT 309 (Implantology) – Mon, Jan 25th (9-11 AM) Exam period Start Date: Mon, Oct 5th, 2026 Exam period End Date: Mon, Jan 25th, 2027 Invigilating exams – 2 invigilators required Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: (AGSEM Invigilator) $18.00 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-01 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
