    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Health-and-Wellness-Advisor_JR0000080012": {
      "title": "Health and Wellness Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Reporting to the Associate Director, Benefits and Disability Management, the incumbent is responsible for the effective delivery of HR services in the areas of Health and Wellness and Benefits. The incumbent will manage the University’s Health and Wellness program and will develop related prevention actions and activities. Acts as an advisor to the University community with respect to the application of procedures and best practices. Works in close collaboration with the Benefits, Disability management and Organizational Development teams and other Universities stakeholders to provide support for the management of the University’s Health and wellness initiatives and priorities as well as any related duties.   Primary Responsibilities: Manage McGill University’s Health and Wellness program, ensuring strategic alignment with organizational priorities and employee needs. Create and implement a comprehensive annual programming calendar, incorporating conferences, communications, and educational content across multiple channels. Develop prevention activities and actions by using various sources of information. Plan, organize, and execute large-scale initiatives such as the annual Health Fair, promoting physical, mental, social, financial, and nutritional wellness. Oversee and continuously enhance the Health and Wellness website, ensuring relevant, accessible, and up-to-date content. Proactively improve the offering in accordance with new trends in wellness. Drive continuous improvement of programs by identifying emerging trends, benchmarking best practices, and introducing innovative approaches to employee wellness. Establish, monitor, and analyze key performance indicators to evaluate program effectiveness and return on investment, and recommend enhancements accordingly. Support, in collaboration with other stakeholders, the University’s efforts to obtain Excellence Canada certification as well as address psychosocial risks and their impact on employee’s psychological health and wellness. Facilitate a cross-functional working group with members of the University HR community to identify priorities, co-create initiatives, and strengthen engagement. Oversee and promote the activities related to the Employee and Family Assistance Program. Build and maintain relationships with internal stakeholders, external partners and service providers. Provides support for the management of the University’s benefit programs. Support the Associate Director, Benefits and Disability Management with other related projects and tasks.   Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Must have minimum 3 years of experience in managing Health and Well-Being programs or in a related position. Experienced in planning and organizing events. Demonstrated ability to develop creative solutions to complex problems. Ability to persuade and influence in adverse situations. Proven ability to analyze HR data and develop strategies to improve programs and reduce costs. Experience working in a unionized environment an asset. Proven team-player with success in building and maintaining strong, consistent, and positive working relationships. Good communication and presentation skills. Ability to work in a computerized environment. Membership in a professional order, such as the Ordre des conseillers en ressources humaines agréés, is an asset. Written and spoken French and English. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #3 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 04) $66,190.00 - $82,740.00 - $99,290.00 Job Profile: MPEX-ADM2A - General Administration - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director Disability Management and Benefits Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-14 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McLennan-Library/Admissions-Administrator_JR0000080001": {
      "title": "Admissions Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Reporting to the Senior Admissions Officer, the incumbent is responsible for making a fixed number of admission decisions per week on assigned undergraduate and graduate applications, certificates, and diploma programs by determining eligibility of applicants and considering multiple sources of information based on predetermined guidelines and procedures. Additionally, directs queries pertaining to scholarships and student aid. Primary Responsibilities: Assist the admissions team during a high-pressure period with the review of student applications for various faculties and schools, determining the eligibility of undergraduate applicants and working with a variety of admit types and programs. Evaluate student files for admission to McGill, considering multiple sources of information, based on established guidelines and procedures and under time constraints. Implement moderately complex administrative procedures or systems in support of the faculty, department, or unit’s operations, ensuring activities meet or exceed established quality standards. Review and make decisions on straightforward admission files; consult with senior staff on complex applications and follow up on missing documentation. Participate in the grade verification process, finalize admission files, and assign transfer credits. Apply information received and select appropriate procedures for conducting admissions, government reporting, recruitment, scholarships, and student record activities. Administer activities related to academic student records and liaise with faculties and units to ensure accuracy and compliance. Establish and foster effective working relationships by identifying needs and providing support in the delivery of services. Assess and resolve administrative issues, informing supervisors and formulating recommendations as necessary. Utilize various systems, including Slate, Banner, and Minerva, to manage and process applications and student records. Attend meetings to discuss admissions processes and policies. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Demonstrates high degree of integrity and work ethics in decision-making. Interprets and judges validity of academic records based on pre-determined criteria. Organized and manages time effectively and efficiently. Works well under pressure by providing outstanding admission service to current and prospective students to meet enrolment targets. Resourceful in remaining current on changes in educational systems and credentials. Maintains the highest level of discretion, compassion, and professionalism. Uses Slate, Banner, Minerva, and complete Microsoft Office Tools effectively.  Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #3 on a scale of 0-4   Please note that the recruitment process for this position may include a testing component following the interview. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III 3 Years Related Experience with DEC III / Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level H) $33.05 - $40.97 Hours per Week: 20 (Part time) Supervisor: Senior Admissions Officer Position End Date (If applicable): 2026-12-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-14 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-1010/Carpenter--Downtown-_JR0000072548-1": {
      "title": "Carpenter (Downtown)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Facilities Management and Ancillary Services - Building Operations Position Summary: Repairs, constructs, modify, makes and installs any wooden fixtures, gypsum walls, fittings or furniture. Installs and repairs door hardware Qualifications: DEP in Carpentry and 5 years of work experience is required. Competency card is an asset. Must have attended a construction safety course and obtained an ASP Construction card. English and French (functional) spoken and read. English or French (functional) written. Hours of Work: 38.75 hrs./week; Monday to Friday from 7:30 am to 3:45 pm. Incumbent will be required to be on 24/7 call-in for one week every 7-10 weeks. K nowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 2 on a scale of 0-4. Hourly Salary: $31.66 Hours per Week: 38.75 (Full time) Location: Sherbrooke 1010 Supervisor: Sector Operations Supervisor Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-11 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Redpath-Library/Casual-Staffing---Operations-Manager_JR0000079809-2": {
      "title": "Casual Staffing & Operations Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Student Accessibility and Achievement provides an array of learner support services to McGill students of all levels of study, including reasonable academic accommodations for those with documented disabilities of either a permanent, temporary, or episodic nature. ​They foster an accessible and inclusive university experience for McGill’s diverse student population in collaboration with other Student Services and the wider McGill community through resources and services.  Additional Information: Overtime, including evening and weekend hours may be required during peak periods. POSITION SUMMARY:  Under the supervision of the Associate Director, Exams & Operations, ensure the seamless integration of human resources services across casual staffing operations at Student Accessibility & Achievement (SAA).  Oversee and approve time entry, record management, and scheduling, ensuring compliance with various Collective Agreements, HR policies, and privacy regulations. Maintain a deep understanding of collective agreements and university policies to drive operational excellence by developing and implementing processes that streamline workflows and enhance service delivery. Lead recruitment, onboarding, and training initiatives. Manage operations, including scheduling hours for a variety of exams and other work. Directly supervise casual employees (e.g., AGSEM, AMUSE) and employees in MUNACA positions. Meet regularly with employees to review work priorities and deadlines, and to provide coaching and training. Consult with Managers regarding performance and set goals and objectives. Approve absences and vacation. Collaborate with key university stakeholders to ensure practices remain innovative, inclusive, and compliant with the latest standards in HR, IT, and financial operations, ensuring that existing administrative and technical procedures and policies are followed PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES Staff Management:  Facilitates communications between managers within the unit and Student Services (S2) HR. Provide guidance to local managers on HR, University, and Service policies and procedures. In consultation with S2 HR, develop and document policies that work within the S2 and the SAA framework. Advise SAA managers on HR activities for non-unionized and unionized groups, including collective agreements. Handle grievances, disputes, and disciplinary matters by gathering appropriate documentation and preparing these for presentation to HR and Labour and Employee Relations (LER). Participate in grievance and arbitration meetings. Assess training needs, develop materials, and deliver training sessions. Lead recruitment for casual exam staff (invigilators, scribes, readers, exam coordinators), including job postings and interviews. Approve and recommend hiring and extension of contracts for all temporary workers within SAA. Develop and review the postings in conjunction with the supervisor to ensure that they reflect the job description and conform with the appropriate collective agreement. Supervise casual exam staff (AMUSE, AGSEM, and non-unionized) providing services to the Exam Centre. Ensure the appropriate staffing supports related to casual and/or student staff are in place to support service needs.  [Approximately 175-200 total staff during the academic year and approximately 75 during summer semester.  During peak periods 400-500 exams per day is common in six to 10 separate buildings on both campuses]. Ensure service standards and policies, particularly confidentiality, are met and followed. Ensure appropriate staffing supports for casual and student staff. Maintain probationary/trial period compliance and prepare notifications to AGSEM related to the hiring of staff as outlined in the AGSEM-Invigilator Collective Agreement.  Receive, investigate and resolve student complaints regarding service policies and procedures as well as the delivery of Exam-related supports.  Resolve issues related to technical service provision and support .  Case Escalation and Referrals: Manage complex escalated cases and inquiries, ensuring appropriate referrals to student support services. Report exceptional incidents to the Associate Director and relevant service areas. Identify crisis situations and initiate the Crisis Management Protocol, as needed. Handle sensitive and confidential inquiries, suggesting solutions and facilitating referrals. Service Delivery & Logistics: Ensure the exam process for students with SAA is respected and efficiently managed. Plan logistics for exams, including staffing, training, space assignments, and room bookings. Oversee the setup of satellite exam offices and provision of supplies. Create, post, and assign shifts for casual staff paying particular attention to the priority pools as outlined in the Collective Agreement(s). Review, verify and approve hour submissions via Workday. Manage exam materials' safe storage, pick-up, and delivery. Review and update exam procedures and process documentation in collaboration with the Exam Center Manager to implement and establish best practices in accommodated exam provision.  Track staff communications, late arrivals, and absences, ensuring records are updated. Ensure that Incident Reports are completed and follow up with casual staff for further information.  Escalate to Exam Systems and Scheduling Manager for follow up with the Associate Deans, etc.  Prepare relevant reports and statistics to be used for projections and planning.  Resource Development and Miscellaneous Duties: Regularly review and update training materials for casual staff to reflect current policies. Develop training on key topics such as handling emergencies, de-escalating situations, and enforcing procedures. Create FAQ pages for casual employees to address common issues. Compose secure communications to students, faculty, and staff to ensure the dissemination of time sensitive information. Maintain relationships with internal and external stakeholders, fostering good public relations. Contribute to special projects under the direction of the Exam Systems and Scheduling Manager and/or Associate Director. Perform duties of the Tutorial Administrator during planned and unplanned absences, as needed. Performs other duties, as assigned.  Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Education, or a related field. Minimum 3-5 years of experience in HR management, staff supervision, or administrative roles, preferably in an academic or student services environment. Strong understanding of HR policies, collective agreements, and labor relations. Proven experience working with collective agreements, unionized and non-unionized staff. Experience managing large-scale logistics, such as exam coordination or event planning, an asset. Familiarity with university governance, particularly in student services and accessibility. Demonstrated ability to take responsibility and deliver results with minimum direction and oversight.  Must be self-directed and able to work autonomously and as part of a team in a fast paced, dynamic and deadline-oriented environment. Knowledge of crisis management protocols and procedures.Experience using de-escalation techniques, strong asset. Proven proficiency in handling crises and initiating appropriate protocols under pressure. Ability to manage escalated cases and inquiries, often of a sensitive or complex nature, and provide effective solutions. Proven ability to recruit, supervise, train, and motivate staff, including resolving conflicts and addressing performance issues. Demonstrated high-level problem solving, organizational and time management skills with a proven ability to manage multiple complex schedules, logistics activities and projects with competing demands and deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to compose professional documents and manage confidential information with tact and diplomacy. High level of emotional intelligence and strong interpersonal skills for interacting with students, faculty, and staff across multiple departments. Meticulous in managing records, schedules, and HR documentation, ensuring accuracy and compliance. Proficient in IT systems related to HR, scheduling, payroll, and record management. Proficient with Microsoft Office Suite, HR systems, and databases for tracking staff performance and records.Demonstrated ability to handle quickly changing priorities, including stepping into additional roles or tasks as needed. Ability to work closely with various stakeholders, including service areas, faculties, and campus services, to ensure smooth operations and maintain positive relationships. Knowledge of French and English. McGill University is an English-language university where day-to-day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 (fluent) on a scale of 0-4. Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 04) $66,190.00 - $82,740.00 - $99,290.00 Job Profile: MPEX-ADM2A - General Administration - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director, Exams & Operations Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-08-31 Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Brown-Student-Serv/Service-Representative_JR0000079890": {
      "title": "Service Representative",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Student Wellness Hub The Student Wellness Hub provides a range of health services to McGill students with a focus on awareness, prevention, and early intervention. The Student Wellness Hub has a variety of clinicians that provide one-on-one appointments, therapy groups and other services. Within the Student Wellness Hub, the Healthy Living Annex focuses on health promotion and offers peer support programs for both the Macdonald and downtown campuses. Position Summary: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, performs duties related to admissions and registration, and student accounts. Provides information and explanations concerning programs, policies and procedures. Processes admission applications, registrations, transcript requests and activities related to student account fee payments. Maintains files and records and resolves related problems. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Provides excellent customer service to all students accessing the student the Wellness Hub.   Acts as the first point of contact for the Hub. Responds to general inquiries; provides information on activities, procedures and services offered, e.g., group counselling, workshops, types of appointments available (physician, nurse, therapist, dietitian, etc.). Responds to emergency walk-in situations as per Hub protocols.   Schedules appointments for professionals. Registers clients for scheduled   professional appointments. Verifies student status and eligibility to use the Hub when making appointments or checking in.     Responsible for the delivery of mail and faxes to appropriate individuals .    Processes requests for “Release of Information” including requesting existing (paper) charts from archives.   Processes debit and credit card payments for no show, late fees and appointment fees as required . I ssues receipts. Closes batch of Moneris transactions at the end of the day.   When necessary, directs clients to alternate Montreal clinics and/or specialists.   Responsible for scanning existing paper files into the electronic record management system. Scans various other documents for inclusion in client f iles.   Provides secretarial support to the unit.    Transmits referrals or other required documents using appropriate methods (faxing, scanning, mailing).   Maintains and enters up to date student information using the electronic medical system . Ensures the accuracy and completeness of information. Investigates and follows up on discrepancies. Consults appropriate documentation or resource persons to obtain and provide information. Resolves problems. Refers complex problems to resource persons.    Explains and demonstrates the use of computerized information systems such as an automated registration system and student accounts system. Provides assistance in completing various forms.    Uses standard office equipment such as computer and photocopier.     Changes signs on door and replenishes ticket dispenser if needed .        Performs other related duties as required .   The list of duties and responsibilities outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks, which may be performed by an employee whose position has been matched to this generic job description. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities:  Must be customer focused and service oriented, which includes but is not limited to being approachable, responsive, attentive and helpful.   Assists all clients with a positive attitude, tact and diplomacy while maintaining a professional manner and competence at all times .   Demonstrated ability to clearly receive, retain and transmit information with a proven ability to communicate clearly and effectively at all levels.   Proven ability to work autonomously and as a member of a team. Demonstrated ability to take initiative, problem- solve and organize work within area of responsibility.   Proven ability to be proactive and devote full attention to clientele. Demonstrated ability to answer calls with professionalism and tact while dealing patiently and calmly with clients who are anxious.   Strong organizational skills with ability to multi-task, prioritize and work under pressure to meet multiple deadlines.   Proven discretion in dealing with confidential information.   Ensure that clients from diverse cultures, ethnic origins, sexual and gender identifications, religious or faith backgrounds and all types of abilities receive equitable treatment and access to Services.   Demonstrated ease with technological applications with a proven ability to work in a PC environment using MS Word, Excel and Outlook.   Demonstrated ability to work with clinical and administrative information systems such as Titanium, Medesync , etc is a very strong asset.   English, spoken and written . French, spoken and read . Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 (fluent) on a scale of 0-4.   Minimum Education and Experience: DEP - Office Systems 3 Years Related Experience / DEP - Secretarial Studies Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level F) $29.42 - $36.46 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Client Service Manager Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-10 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McLennan-Library/Convocation-Clerk_JR0000080040": {
      "title": "Convocation Clerk",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Convocation Clerk   The Convocation clerk plays an important role during McGill University’s Convocation ceremonies and is primarily responsible for the distribution of line up cards, tickets, and important information to graduates.   Among other related duties, provides support with various convocation activities and related services and acts as a resource agent for graduates and guests.   It is essential that Convocation clerks respond well to stressful situations and maintain the utmost composure and courtesy. Qualifications:   Candidates must be customer focused and service oriented with a proven ability to communicate clearly and effectively at all levels. Demonstrated ability to clearly receive, retain and transmit information. Proven organizational skills, multi-tasking, accuracy and attention to detail.  Ability to work autonomously and as a member of a team.  Demonstrated ability to problem solve and work under pressure.   Hiring Unit:   Enrolment Services   Reporting to:     Clara Spadafora, Assistant Registrar Convocation and Communication, Enrolment Services   Schedule: Week of 12 October 2026 Wednesday, 14 October 2026 - Training Meeting (12:00 p.m. – 1:00 p.m.) Friday, 16 October 2026 (10:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.) At the McGill Campus Store Week of 19 October 2026             Monday, 19 October 2026 (7:30 a.m. – 2:30 p.m.)   at the McGill Campus Store - 680 Rue Sherbrooke O, Montreal QC H3A or Monday, 19 October 2026 (8:30 a.m. – 3:30 p.m.) at the Convocation venue: Place des Arts - 175 Rue Sainte-Catherine, Montréal, QC H2X 3X5, Canada Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 3(qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma Minimal or No Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE A) $16.70 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 20 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-10-14 Position End Date: 2026-10-20 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-20 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
