    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Various/Invigilator---SPOT-Midterm-Exam_JR0000080022-1": {
      "title": "Invigilator - SPOT Midterm Exam",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: School of Physical and Occupational Therapy Exam Dates/Times (including additional time): PHTH 301/Written 14 September 13h30-14h30 (arrival 13h00) Number of Positions: 1 Locations: Various Instructors: TBD Position Summary: Responsible for setting up the examination room according to specific requirements as well as ensuring that equipment and facilities are functioning properly. Administers the delivery of the electronic and paper exams and documentation accordingly. Handles students’ issues and directs them to IT support, the Exam Administrator or Professor as needed. Ensures that students comply with regulations with respect to the exam. Responsible to report any behavior by students or others that does not comply with University regulations. Ensures that all mobile and web‐accessible electronic devices are collected from the students prior to the start of the examination and returned upon their departure. Ensures that students are accompanied to the washroom. Alerts the Professor or Exam Administrator when students have a question. At the end of the examination period, collects all exam materials and ensures nothing is left behind in the examination room(s). Responsible for reporting back to the Professor or Exam Administrator and ensuring delivery of the exams. Qualifications: High School Leaving Certificate/Diploma (minimum requirement). Hourly Salary: (AGSEM Invigilator) $18.00 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-09 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Stewart-Biology-Bldg/Assistant-Professor-in-Quantitative-Cell-Biology---Department-of-Biology_JR0000079704": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Quantitative Cell Biology - Department of Biology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n​ Please refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Biology Position Description: The Department of Biology at McGill University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in quantitative cell biology with a target start date of August 1, 2027. The ideal candidate will develop an innovative, interdisciplinary research program using modern molecular and cell biology approaches together with advanced quantitative analysis, computational modeling, and AI-driven methodologies to address fundamental questions in biology. We welcome candidates whose research programs will also seek to understand how molecular and cellular processes shape health and/or contribute to a sustainable environment . The department offers access to a host of advanced microscopy resources, such as light sheet , super-resolution, and advanced confocal microscopy. Through state-of-the-art core facilities, McGill University offers atomic-resolution cryo-electron microscopy, mass spectrometry, next-generation sequencing, and plant and animal facilities, among others. Overall, the department provides a unique and stimulating research environment that is highly conducive to collaboration and interdisciplinary approaches. In addition to its research mission, the Department of Biology plays a key role in undergraduate education in the biological and biomedical sciences. Faculty will have the opportunity to supervise and mentor graduate students in the Biology, Biochemistry, Biophysics, Quantitative Life Sciences, and Integrated Program in Neuroscience programs.   About us : McGill University is a leading research university in Canada. Its downtown campus sits at the foot of Mont Royal, a large green space overlooking the heart of Downtown Montréal. A UNESCO City of Design, Montréal is world-renowned for its high quality of life and arts, design, food, and festivals. Despite its global reputation, the city is one of the most affordable and livable large metropolitan areas in Canada and the US.   Job Duties: The successful applicant will be expected to conduct a rigorous program of independent, externally funded research. The successful applicant will also contribute to teaching in the Biology core curriculum, which includes foundational courses in undergraduate molecular biology and cell biology, as well as courses offered through joint programs and at the graduate level. Preference will be given to applicants who can demonstrate a commitment to teaching a diverse student body.   Qualifications and Education Requirements: Applicants must possess a Ph.D. or equivalent degree in Biology or a related discipline, as well as postdoctoral experience and a significant track record of research excellence as demonstrated by scientific publications.   Faculty/Department/Unit: Science/Biology Job Type: Tenure-track Rank: Assistant Professor Salary: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Posting Period: To ensure full consideration, complete applications should be received by October 12, 2026. Contact: Enquiries should be directed to Rodrigo Reyes at info.biology@mcgill.ca     Required Documents: Persons wishing to be considered for this position should provide a one-page summary of the application package (briefly describing academic background, major research contributions, and teaching experience) ; a curriculum vitae (including a list of publications) ; a research statement i ncluding previous contributions and future plans , as well as any leaves contributing to career interruptions or slowdowns (maximum 3 pages); a statement of teaching philosophy and experience , including an account of a commitment to inclusive teaching, learning and supervision (maximum 1 page ), and PDF files of up to 3 major publications. After submitting your application, you may be contacted to provide the name and email address of at least three referees, who can provide confidential letters to accompany your application.   Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
