    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Res-Carrefour-Sherb/Protection-Supervisor_JR0000070006": {
      "title": "Protection Supervisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Student Housing & Hospitality Services Position Summary: Reporting to the Associate Director Protection, Student Housing & Hospitality Services, the Protection Supervisor is responsible for the day-to-day operations by directing a team of Night Stewards within the Unit. Provides the best possible direction of comprehensive programs related to security services, emergency preparedness, fire prevention and environmental health and safety in an environment that fosters a sense of community, enhances student learning/safety and supports the overall mission of the SHHS unit within the University. Fosters a safe and healthy environment for students, staff and visitors while enforcing policies, procedures, legislation and regulations concerning building access control, thefts and incidents, accidents and safety training. Primary Responsibilities: Directly supervise the team of approximately 10 to 20 Night Stewards and casuals, including participating in the hiring, interviewing. Make recommendations on probation or bring up issues to the Associate Director Protection. Train and coach staff and organize activities to support the day/night operations of the unit by ensuring that functions are carried out in accordance with established goals and objectives. Implement administrative procedures in support of the unit's operation. Assist with the organization of security , fire protection, safety, environmental and occupational health programs, are adminsitered in conformity with established procedures and guidelines. Participate in public awareness activities by promoting the services offered. . Plan and oversee the implementation of projects. Participate in the writing of documents or reports related to issues (e.g. security, emergency measure, fire prevention, environmental health and safety, access control, etc.). Administer safety inspections of the unit's buildings, as per legislation and regulations. When appropriate, inform the Associate Director Protection of discrepancies and formulate recommendations. Provide support /resources/assistance to the communities for security and /or safety concerns. Provide assistance and liaise with University Safety office related to queries from internals and externals. Support emergency response operations and emergency preparedness program protocol; and respond to incidents in accordance with response procedures and communicated directives. Establish the work schedule on a rotational basis. Ensure back-up list is available in case of Night Steward vacation or unplanned leave. Establish and foster effective working relationships by identifying needs and providing support in the delivery of services. Produces quarterly reports/monthly evaluations and presents it to the Associate Director Protection for review. Assist employees in their training. Conducts rounds/patrols(overnight) within the SHHS, including Solin Hall. Strong knowledge of Collective Union Agreements. Minimum Education & Experience: DEC III Three (3) years' related experience Other Qualifying Skills And/Or Abilities: Required: Security Permit (BSP) and First Aid. Experience in the support, training and supervision of staff. Experience in a security environment, particularly working in a university student residence operation. Demonstrated ability to supervise unionized staff as well as able to interpret collective agreements. Proven organizational and leadership skills along with excellent interpersonal, communication and problem-solving skills. Ability to work as part of a team. Proven ability to adapt to flexible year round schedules. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in French and English. Additional Information: This is an overnight position (Sunday, Monday, Thursday, Friday & Saturday 21h00 to 5h00, may be subject to change). Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 on a scale of 0-4. Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 03) $63,350.00 - $74,530.00 - $85,710.00 Job Profile: MPEX-LOG1B - Security, Safety & Environment - Professional 1 (Excluded) Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Sunday, Monday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday Supervisor: Associate Director Protection Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-30 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Currie-Gymnasium/Technical-Specialist---Assistant-Coach-Martlet-Basketball_JR0000079690": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist - Assistant Coach Martlet Basketball",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Position Summary: Under the direction of the Martlet Basketball Head Coach, the technical specialist - Assistant Coach will assist the full-time staff with various duties related to the administration, training, and competing of the women's basketball program. Primary Responsibilities: Record activities during a game and keep track of statistics. Analyze data and identify game/team/athlete activity/competency trends during the game and post-game. Compile statistics and produce reports for the coaching staff to review Assist in practices and off-season workouts with individual skill development Support coaching staff in the implementation of practice and game plans. Assist with the maintenance and distribution of on-field team equipment. Assist with practices and off-season workouts with individual skill development, implementation of practice and game plans. Assist coaching staff with various administrative tasks as required. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities NCCP Level II Certification (Basketball) or equivalent required Coaching experience at the elite and/or competitive level required Knowledge of or prior practical experience in the sport of basketball required Strong organizational skills with the ability to multitask and work in a team-oriented environment Punctuality, reliability, and a strong work ethic are required. Bilingual in French and English ***Safe Sport and CCES Anti-doping training and coursework are mandatory ***Selected candidates must successfully pass their criminal background check. Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $17.17 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 20 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-08-03 Position End Date: 2027-04-15 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-10 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Currie-Gymnasium/Technical-Specialist---Assistant-Coach-Martlet-Hockey_JR0000079942": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist - Assistant Coach Martlet Hockey",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Athletics & Recreation Primary Responsibilities: Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, the Technical Specialist will assist in implementing performance and student-athlete development initiatives that support the success of the Martlets hockey program. The incumbent will provide technical, analytical, and operational support to the coaching staff and contribute to the overall development of the program. Primary Responsibilities Review video analysis following games and practices, identifying trends, strengths, and areas for improvement. Prepare opposition pre-scout reports, including player and team tendencies. Support the coaching staff in the planning and execution of practices, games, and athlete development initiatives. Record game activities and maintain statistical data. Analyze individual and team performance metrics and prepare reports for the coaching staff. Assist with the preparation, organization, maintenance, and distribution of team equipment for practices and games. Assist with gameday and practice operations to ensure a high-performance training environment. Provide technical and administrative support related to athlete performance and team operations. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Knowledge of and/or previous practical experience in high-performance hockey. Demonstrated coaching, technical, video analysis, or athlete development skills in hockey. Strong organizational, communication, and time-management skills. Detail-oriented, dependable, punctual, and team-oriented. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Experience with video analysis software and performance analysis tools is considered an asset. NCCP Level II certification or equivalent is considered an asset. Bilingual - French and English ***Safe Sport and CCES Anti-doping training and coursework are mandatory ***Selected candidates must successfully pass their criminal background check. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 3 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE D) $40.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 20 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-08-31 Position End Date: 2027-04-15 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-10 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Currie-Gymnasium/Technical-Specialist-Assistant-Coach-Martlet-Soccer_JR0000079904": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist Assistant Coach Martlet Soccer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary Under the direction of the Head Coach Martlet Soccer, the Assistant Coach / Technical Specialist Martlets Soccer will support the Head Coach in the delivery of a high-performance women’s soccer program within McGill Athletics & Recreation. This role will contribute to the daily training environment, competition preparation, and administrative operations, with a strong emphasis on student-athlete development, performance analysis, and alignment with RSEQ/U SPORTS and McGill standards of excellence. Primary Duties: Assist in the planning and delivery of a comprehensive, high-performance training program for McGill Martlets Women’s Soccer. Review video analysis operations, including post-match breakdowns, individual athlete feedback, and opposition scouting reports (pre-scouts) within the RSEQ/U SPORTS context. Assist in analyzing match and training data to identify team and individual performance trends Prepare detailed reports and actionable insights for coaching staff. Record match statistics and maintain performance tracking systems during competitions. Assist in the implementation of tactical game plans and practice objectives in collaboration with the coaching staff. Oversee the preparation, organization, and distribution of training and match equipment, ensuring professional standards consistent with varsity sport. Support team operations on game days, including ensuring bench assignments, communication, and logistics. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities NCCP Level II Certification (or equivalent recognized coaching certification) required Strong knowledge of women’s soccer at the U SPORTS / RSEQ or equivalent high-performance level preferred Demonstrated coaching experience in competitive or elite women’s soccer, preferably at the university, provincial, or national level required Detail-oriented with strong analytical and video breakdown capabilities required Team-oriented mindset with a strong work ethic. Excellent organizational, communication, and time-management skills preferred Ability to work effectively within a student focused and, academically intensive environment preferred Bilingual in French and English (verbal and written) required ***Safe Sport and CCES Anti-doping training and coursework are mandatory ***Selected candidates must successfully pass their criminal background check. Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE C) $20.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 10 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-08-24 Position End Date: 2027-04-16 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-10 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Office-Assistant-A_JR0000079825": {
      "title": "Office Assistant A",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Internships & Student Affairs Office Position Summary: This is a Work study position. Only McGill University students who are currently enrolled in a program (excluding Faculty of Education program) are eligible to apply. Applicants must be Work Study Program eligible. Primary Duties Attending to the front desk, giving information to visitors , and directing them as required Answering e-mails and phone calls in a timely & professional manner Following up with different parties by email. Organizing digital files. General clerical duties, including filing, photocopying, shredding, etc. Assisting with special events and projects during the course of normal working hours. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Excellent customer service skills. Excellent communication skills, both oral and written. Good knowledge of McGill's campus, services and resources. Ability to be focused and flexible, and work in a busy environment. Ability to work in a PC environment. Basic web editing experience is an asset. Punctual, organized and professional. Good command of English is required; French is an asset. Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma Minimal or No Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE A) $17.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 12 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-08-30 Position End Date: 2026-12-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-13 This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
