    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Montreal-Neuro/Clinical-Research-Coordinator_JR0000079248": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: To coordinate and advance CAPTURE ALS research activities at the Montreal Neurological Institute (The Neuro), ensuring operational excellence, regulatory compliance, participant engagement, and national collaboration across the CAPTURE ALS platform. Primary Responsibilities:   Research Operations & Coordination Coordinate day-to-day CAPTURE ALS activities at The Neuro, ensuring support of study visits, recruitment targets, and project milestones. Support Investigators/Physicians and the national CAPTURE ALS team in setting priorities and timelines. Record and administer participant information, and carry out required study visit activities in collaboration with medical staff. Attend and contribute to internal and external meetings, including the CAPTURE ALS Coordinators Committee. Serve as liaison between researchers, participants, the Clinical Research Manager and the Program Manager. Data, Sample & Regulatory Oversight Maintain study documentation (e.g., Investigator Site Files, source documents) and ensure regulatory compliance. Coordinate ethics submissions, amendments, and updates with the Research Ethics Board. Oversee data and sample workflows in collaboration with CBIG and LORIS teams, ensuring quality control and monitoring. Contribute to the development and maintenance of SOPs, policies, and internal guidelines. Conduct or support sample collection activities (as applicable and licensed). Platform Development, Reporting & Strategic Support Support participant engagement, outreach, and presentations to promote CAPTURE ALS and disseminate results. Prepare project reports and contribute to budget planning and financial tracking. Assist in drafting grant proposals, project proposals, publications, and communication materials. Build and maintain strong relationships with internal and external partners. Support identification and pursuit of funding and revenue-generating opportunities. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities Undergraduate Degree in Biology or Sciences required. Fluent in French and English required. Two years clinical research experience required. Previous experience with patients required. Proven organizational skills. Must be able to manage multiple activities and projects simultaneously. Ability to troubleshoot, solve problems, take initiative, and prioritize work. Team player. At ease with technology and troubleshooting tech-related problems. Experience with elderly, mobility-reduced, and other vulnerable patient populations an asset. As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III 3 Years Related Experience / Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level H) $33.05 - $40.97 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Program Manager Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-08-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-11 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
