    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Adams-Building/Senior-Entrepreneurship-Advisor_JR0000077121": {
      "title": "Senior Entrepreneurship Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Senior Entrepreneurship Advisor - Digital Health This is a one-year, part-time term position, with the possibility of renewal. Salary will be pro-rated according to hours worked . The position is based in the McGill Engine Centre ( https://www.mcgill.ca/engine/),  in collaboration with the Clinical Innovation Platform at the Research Institute of the McGill University Health Centre (CLIP - https://rimuhc.ca/clinical-research/clinical-innovation-platform-clip ). Responsibilities and activities align with those of an Entrepreneur‑in‑Residence , mentoring program participants, evaluating project submissions, and providing professional expertise on the potential commercialization of their technologically-based ideas. The location of work will be evenly split between McGill and CLIP. Position Summary: McGill Engine in collaboration with the CLIP is launching the new “Health Innovations Catalyst” (“InnovSanté”) program, for multidisciplinary research teams from Quebec universities and their affiliated hospitals and research institutes interested in commercializing their research in the fields of: therapeutics, diagnostics, digital health, surgical tools, tools for drug discovery and development, and medical devices. We aim to accelerate and increase the number of innovative startups in the fields of medtech and life sciences in Quebec by creating a unique, tailored, and favorable ecosystem of all essential stakeholders. Senior Entrepreneurship Advisors will be selected from three different industry verticals, namely medtech, digital health, and life sciences/biotech. They will function as Entrepreneurs-in-Residence , providing practical guidance, coaching and mentoring to Quebec university researchers, inventors, students, and startup teams as they pursue their health-related innovation entrepreneurial journeys. Primary Responsibilities: Assist in the development and promotion of the InnovSanté program, specifically in the filed of Digital Health Meet one-on-one with potential team program participants to provide professional expertise on the potential commercialization of their technologically-based ideas, inventions, technologies, R&D projects, and startups/spinoffs that can be applied to health Identify early-stage technologies and teams with commercial potential Evaluate project submissions to the program Take part in the selection process with the Steering Committee Mentor the InnovSanté teams via the lean start-up methodology and the IRL framework, in particular, with each team, set up and keep track of the project development plan, by each IRL indicator Provide one-on-one weekly mentoring meetings with the InnovSanté teams Provide expertise on team composition, links with key project stakeholders, and project funding opportunities from other existing programs (preclinical work, user evaluations, or pilot projects to demonstrate performance and/or technology scale-up) Facilitate connections of InnovSanté teams to other program support resources (internal and external), in particular clinicians and MBA student interns Provide contacts and introductions for the InnovSanté teams to the program network partners (industry experts via MEDTEQ and Consortium Québécois sur la Découverte du Médicament, and investors such as adMare, Fonds FTQ, Lumira, Genesys, Amplitude) as part of their project development plan Collaborate with other business incubators, business accelerators and other entrepreneurial support organizations inside and outside of McGill, e.g., the Dobson Centre, Centech, L’Esplanade, etc. Assist with technology transfer, licensing and industrial partnerships Provide educational workshops on topics related to health-related technological innovation and entrepreneurship Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Proven track record of founding, scaling, or leading digital health startups Minimum 8–10 years of experience in healthcare technology, telemedicine, health data analytics, or related sectors Strong network within digital health industry, investors, and business accelerators Familiarity with clinical workflows and integration of digital solutions in healthcare delivery Experience in regulatory pathways (Health Canada, FDA, EMA) Visionary thinker passionate about transforming healthcare through innovation Collaborative and approachable, with a commitment to fostering an inclusive and dynamic innovation environment Adaptable to academic settings while maintaining strong industry and investor connections Assets : Graduate degree in a relevant field (e.g., Health Informatics, Biomedical Engineering, Public Health, Business Administration, or related discipline) Demonstrated ability to raise capital, build strategic partnerships, and scale digital health solutions Prior experience as an Entrepreneur-in-Residence, advisor, or mentor in an academic or incubator setting Experience with intellectual property strategy and commercialization within university ecosystems As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 5 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 06) $82,280.00 - $102,850.00 - $123,420.00 Job Profile: MPEX-COM3A - Internal External Relations - Senior Professional/Manager Hours per Week: 20.25 (Part time) Monday, Wednesday, Friday Supervisor: Associate Director ENGINE Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-07-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-11 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Duff-Medical-Bldg/Research-Associate_JR0000079870": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary Research Program Development Develop and conduct research projects, protocols, methodologies and standardized procedures supporting BRAVO research objectives. Design and implement innovative research methods and quality monitoring approaches for advanced therapeutics and organoid biomanufacturing. Analyze and interpret research data and prepare scientific reports, publications and presentations. Ensure the quality, integrity and reproducibility of research activities and outcomes. Research Coordination and Infrastructure Coordinate the implementation of BRAVO research infrastructure across participating institutions. Collaborate with investigators, partner institutions and technical personnel to support research infrastructure integration. Participate in equipment evaluation, procurement, qualification and implementation activities. Develop and maintain Quality Management System (QMS) procedures and monitor project milestones to support research objectives. Research Leadership and Knowledge Translation Provide functional supervision, guidance and training to Research Assistants, trainees and technical personnel. Develop standardized research procedures and promote collaboration across multidisciplinary teams. Disseminate research findings through publications, presentations, reports and stakeholder engagement. Prepare grant applications, progress reports and other scientific documentation. Strategic Research Development Establish collaborative partnerships with academic, clinical, government and industry stakeholders. Participate in provincial and national research networks supporting advanced therapeutics and regenerative medicine. Contribute to the sustainability and continuous improvement of BRAVO research programs and infrastructure. Support strategic planning and identify future research and funding opportunities. Qualifications PhD in Bioengineering, Biomedical Sciences, Chemical Engineering, Biological Sciences, or a related field, with at least 5 years of related research experience . Experience in one or more of the following areas: advanced therapeutics, organoid technologies, biomanufacturing, or GLP/GMP-regulated research. Demonstrated experience developing research methods, analyzing scientific data, preparing publications, and contributing to grant applications. Strong scientific writing, analytical, organizational, interpersonal, and research coordination skills. Excellent written and spoken English; French is an asset. Assets: Experience in translational research, technology transfer, or the biopharmaceutical sector. Experience supervising or training research personnel. Certification or training in Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP) or stem cell research (e.g., CASTL, CATTI, NIBRT, EATRIS, ASQ, GpX, Stem Cell Network, ISCT, or ISSCR). Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4. Hourly Salary: $35.37 Hours per Week: 35 (Full time) Location: Duff Medical Bldg. Supervisor: Professor Position Start Date: 2026-10-26 Position End Date: 2027-10-25 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-05 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Various/Course-Lecturer-EDPE-300-760-762-OFNIE-F26_JR0000079873": {
      "title": "Course Lecturer EDPE 300 760/762 OFNIE F26",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Office of First Nations and Inuit Education (OFNIE) Course Number-Section and Title:  EDPE 300 760/762 Educational Psychology    Course Description: Ed Psych & Couns (Psychology): Selected theories, models, and concepts relevant to planning and reflecting upon educational practice and improvement. Overview of development, learning, thinking, motivation, individual difference, etc. In relation to applications in classroom teaching and learning, the complementary role of counsellors and psychologists, educational computing and technology. The Youth Protection Act. Posting Dates : August 27 - September 9, 2026 Application Deadline: September 9, 2026; 11:59 pm CL Credits: 3 (This course is not team-taught) Number of Positions Available: 2 Term: Fall 2026 Course Dates : October 26 - November 20, 2026 Contract dates : October 12 - December 4, 2026 Schedule: Monday, Tuesday, & Thursday; 6:00 pm - 9:15 pm Location: Kahnawà:ke Teaching Qualification Requirements   Education   Master’s or PhD in Educational Psychology, Applied Cognitive Psychology, Learning Sciences, Human Development, or equivalent.   In exceptional circumstances, applicants without a Master’s degree but with significant research or professional experience related to the course content may be considered.   Experience   Knowledge of educational and psychological theories.   Knowledge of the application of educational and psychological theories to authentic settings.   Experience in college/university teaching in this subject or professional experience in teaching K-12.   Knowledge of Ministère de l’Éducation et de l’Enseignement supérieur (MELS) requirements.   Other   Adherence to evolving program requirements concerning course content and program-developed competencies; course content and references must reflect the most current advances in the field.   OFNIE Additional Requirements   Knowledge of the concepts of Inclusive Education.   Training and experience working in schools with students with diverse needs.   Expert knowledge of course content as outlined in the course description.   Knowledge of the Quebec Education Program (QEP) and the curriculum of the partnering school board with whom this course is being delivered.   Familiarity with the 13 professional competencies specified by the Ministère de l’Éducation .   Knowledge of the impact of colonialism on Indigenous communities and a demonstrated ability to integrate pedagogical approaches grounded in equity, diversity, inclusion, and Indigenous perspectives.   Experience as a teacher, administrator, or consultant in the partnering school system for which the course is being delivered.   Experience teaching in the Quebec elementary school system.   Previous successful experience teaching similar courses to pre-service teachers.   Previous successful experience teaching similar courses in Indigenous communities.   Experience developing curriculum, instructional approaches, and/or policy grounded in Indigenous knowledge and pedagogies.   Demonstrated capacity and willingness to adapt course content to the educational, social, cultural, and linguistic context of the community in which the course is being delivered.   Availability to participate in course coordination and planning activities prior to the course start date (approximately two weeks in advance, online).   Information supplémentaires/Additional Information:   Effective dates of the appointment are October 12 - December 4, 2026. Course dates are October 26 - November 26, 2026. This course will be offered in person in Kahnawà:ke  following the schedule above. You are covered by the working conditions specified in the McGill Course Lecturers and Instructors Union collective agreement; https://www.mcgill.ca/hr/files/hr/mcliu_collective_agreement_-_final_version_for_printing_0.pdf . McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English Language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing.  Please contact ofnie.education@mcgill.ca  with any questions you may have. Hiring Unit: Bureau de l’éducation des Premières Nations et des Inuit (OFNIE) Course Title: Psychologie de l’éducation Subject Code: EDPE 300 760/762 Location: Kahnawà:ke Schedule: Lundi, mardi et jeudi; de 18 h à 21 h 15 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-09 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
