    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Various/Office-Assistant-C_JR0000079863": {
      "title": "Office Assistant C",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Under the direction of the immediate supervisor, the incumbent may perform some or all of the listed general administration functions. These functions are of high complexity and the incumbent performs them using general instruction. Hiring Unit: Student Housing & Hospitality Services Position Summary: Acts as a liaison between the unit and internal or external parties to provide various assistance or information; creates reports. The list of functions outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an incumbent. For example, incumbents may be asked to perform some elements of Communications Assistant level “A” and/or “B” in addition to the above listed functions OTHER QUALIFICATIONS: Able to provide essential support in both technical and administrative areas. Ability to interact with people at all levels and deal effectively and diplomatically in all situations. Task includes survey/documentation/inventory of room usage, floor size, ceiling, wall materials; furniture, equipment (such as AC, oven, toilet, etc.) within our buildings in SHHS.  Demonstrated ability to transmit and receive information accurately. Proven organizational skills and ability to prioritize and multi-task. Demonstrated ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Attention to detail. At ease working in a PC environment.  Knowledge of French and English. McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION: Amuse Fall 2026/Winter 2027 position, from August 30, 2026 to May 15, 2027. Work Schedule will be Monday to Friday 9h00 - 17h00 (days and hours may vary upon needs) Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 2 Years Related Experience Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 15 (Part time) Position Start Date: August 30, 2026 Position End Date: May 15, 2027 Hourly Rate: $21.00 Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . McGill University is committed to equity and diversity within its community and values academic rigour and excellence. We welcome and encourage applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to engage productively with diverse communities. At McGill, research that reflects diverse intellectual traditions, methodologies, and modes of dissemination and translation is valued and encouraged. Candidates are invited to demonstrate their research impact both within and across academic disciplines and in other sectors, such as government, communities, or industry. McGill further recognizes and fairly considers the impact of leaves (e.g., family care or health-related) that may contribute to career interruptions or slowdowns. Candidates are encouraged to signal any leave that affected productivity, or that may have had an effect on their career path. This information will be considered to ensure the equitable assessment of the candidate’s record. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated equity groups to self-identify. It further seeks to ensure the equitable treatment and full inclusion of persons with disabilities by striving for the implementation of universal design principles transversally, across all facets of the University community, and through  accommodation policies and procedures . Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Communications-Assistant---Social-Media_JR0000079674": {
      "title": "Communications Assistant - Social Media",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Please note that this is a Work Study Position Position Summary The Faculty of Education is looking for a creative, social-media-savvy student to help us tell the stories of our community and strengthen the Faculty's presence across its social media channels. Working directly under the supervision of the Senior Advisor Transformation and Culture, you will help identify and create engaging content that highlights our students, professors and researchers, academic initiatives, events, accomplishments, and student experience. We are looking for someone who understands how people use social media today and who can uphold high quality and consistent standards, bring fresh ideas, good judgment, and a coherent visual identity to our channels. This is an opportunity to gain hands-on professional experience while building a portfolio of social media content in a university environment. Responsibilities Create and publish engaging social media content, including written copy, basic graphic design, Reels, Stories, and other short-form video content under the direction and supervision of the Senior Advisor Transformation and Culture. Help tell the stories of Faculty of Education students, faculty members, researchers, programs, initiatives, and events. Monitor student and/or community-led social media takeovers initiatives, including identifying students, liaising with them, planning and reviewing their work.   Identify opportunities to highlight student voices and the student experience. Assist with content coordination, planning, scheduling and publishing through platforms and tools such as Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube, Buffer, and other relevant channels. Monitor the Faculty's social media channels and identify relevant content that could be shared or amplified. Help grow and engage the Faculty's audiences through thoughtful, goal-oriented content. Monitor comments and direct messages and direct inquiries to the appropriate Faculty webpages or staff members. Monitor social media platforms for trolling, hate speech, misinformation, and other inappropriate or harmful content. Escalate content that does not comply with Faculty or University equity, safety, and related policies to the direct supervisor. Monitor content published by social media delegates across Faculty units to ensure consistency with the visual identity, tone, quality standards, and guidelines of both the Faculty and McGill University. Apply strong proofreading and quality-control skills, including grammar, spelling, word-count management, accuracy, formatting, image and video resolution, and platform-specific content requirements. Assist with Faculty website edits and updates from time to time. Capture and edit photos and short videos for social media. Keep up with current social media formats, trends, tools, and best practices. Provide platform-based analytics and reports. Ensure content is accurate and consistent with Faculty and University branding and messaging. Other related communications tasks as required. Qualifications Strong understanding of current social media usage, platforms, formats, trends, and online culture. Proven experience with organization accounts on Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube, Buffer, and other relevant channels. Creativity and a strong instinct for what makes social content engaging. Experience creating social media content, including basic graphic design, copywriting, and video editing. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Suite and experience with photography and video production are required. Strong time-management skills. Strong proofreading and quality-control skills, with excellent attention to accuracy, consistency, word count, formatting, and visual quality. Sound judgment and awareness of social media risks, including the ability to identify and appropriately escalate hate speech, misinformation, trolling, and other harmful or inappropriate content. Strong understanding of social media, branding, and visual identity standards Ability to ensure content is consistent with Faculty and University safety policy and guidelines. Self-starter who can work independently while taking direction and feedback. High-level proficiency in written French, including grammar. With your application: please include examples of social media content you have created or a link to an account you currently manage or have managed in the past. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 1 Year Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE B) $27.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 20 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-09-14 Position End Date: 2027-12-31 Deadline to Apply: This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/Communications-Assistant---Graphic-Design_JR0000079752": {
      "title": "Communications Assistant - Graphic Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary The Faculty of Education is looking for a creative student with strong graphic design skills to help produce quality, engaging, and visually consistent communications materials for the Faculty's myriad of initiatives. Working directly under the supervision of the Senior Advisor Transformation and Culture, you will be involved in the development of a new graphic visual identity for the Faculty, creating materials that can be used for recurring and one-off purposes, with templates for both print and digital use. We are looking for someone with strong technical skills who can work within established McGill branding standards while bringing creativity and editorial sense to the Faculty. This is an opportunity to gain professional design experience, work on a wide variety of projects, and build a portfolio of communications materials produced in a university environment. Responsibilities Translate communications needs from the Supervisor and supplied information into clear, consistent, and inspired proposals. Design and edit promotional and communications materials for the Faculty, and at times for its departments and offices, for both digital engagement (social media, websites, display screens in physical spaces, etc.) and print. Produce materials such as logos, posters and flyers, brochures, invitations, eblasts, digital screen displays, reports, presentation documents (Canva, PowerPoint, etc.), and other print and digital assets. Liaise with different units under the supervision of the Senior Advisor Transformation and Culture to develop materials for them or assist them in their own work. Edit and organize a databank of assets, including graphic and motion designs, photographs and stock images, sounds and videos for use across Faculty communications efforts. Adapt existing designs and materials for different formats, audiences, and communications channels. Ensure consistency with McGill and Faculty branding, messaging, and visual standards. Review materials carefully for visual consistency, accuracy, and accessibility. Work with Faculty staff to gather the information and materials needed to complete design projects. Organize design files and assets so that they can be easily accessed and reused by unit delegates and other specific stakeholders. Keep up to date with contemporary graphic design practices and the software and tools needed to produce effective communications materials. Assist with photography, image, sound, and video editing, or other related visual communications tasks as needed. Assist with the physical posting of print materials across all Education Buildings. Other related communications tasks as required. Qualifications Strong graphic design skills and good editorial judgment within an institutional context. Ability to work quickly and prioritize competing demands. Demonstrated ability to create effective materials for both digital and print environments. Proven skills in Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, Lightroom, Premiere, Audition). Proven Canva skills. Excellent and reliable attention to visual detail, including typography, layout, visual hierarchy, consistency, and accuracy. Ability to work within established branding guidelines while still producing engaging and creative work. Reliable and organized, with the ability to manage several projects, liaise with stakeholders with competing needs, and meet deadlines. Ability to work independently and effectively while communicating questions to the supervisor before moving forward with final outputs, taking direction, and incorporating feedback. Photography or video production experience is an asset. Familiarity with accessibility considerations in digital communications is an asset. High-level proficiency in written French, including grammar. Only applications that include a portfolio and examples of graphic design work that demonstrate your graphic design experience and skills will be considered.   Work study letter required. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma 1 Year Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE B) $27.00 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 20 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-09-14 Position End Date: 2026-12-31 Deadline to Apply: This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Education-Building/IT-Assistant-A---AV-Loan-Services_JR0000079732-1": {
      "title": "IT Assistant A - AV Loan Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Primary duties include: The IT Assistant A will assist students and staff using the Faculty of Education AV (audio/visual) Loans Centre. Depending upon assigned shift, open the AV Loan Centre in the morning and close it in the evening Help students, academic staff, and support staff with basic use of computers, presentation equipment, video and audio recording equipment, and other audiovisual equipment as required Maintain an \"alert presence\" in the AV Loan Centre Operate the AV loan service by creating reservations and processing checkouts and returns using our asset management software Web checkout Keep track of the AV Loan equipment inventory Understand the basic operating fundamentals of the AV loan equipment and provide practical tips and operations advice to clientele. Loan Psychology testing kits to ECP students following the AMRC protocols Other related duties as required Preferred Skills/Experience: Previous experience interacting with people in a customer service or assisting role Familiar with the use of computers, presentation equipment, video, and audio equipment General knowledge of common computer software Familiar with asset management software is an asset Reliable, punctual and professional with good communication skills Fluent in English (written and spoken), some basic French (spoken) is an asset Eligibility Requirements Must be eligible to work in Canada Required: Work Study eligible for the 2026-2027 academic year - PLEASE SUBMIT WORKSTUDY APPROVAL LETTER WITH APPLICATION - Current McGill student who will be enrolled in a degree program for the 2026-2027 academic year Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # (qualifier) on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: High School Diploma Minimal or No Related Experience Hourly Salary: (AMUSE A) $16.70 Estimated Number of Work Hours per Week: 12 (Part time) Position Start Date: 2026-09-01 Position End Date: 2027-04-30 Deadline to Apply: This position is covered by the AMUSE collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McIntyre--Medical/Research-Assistant-1_JR0000079795-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant 1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Under the supervision of Prof. Gergely Lukacs the Research Assistant will be responsible for supporting laboratory research activities, including: Cloning, mutagenesis, expression and membrane and chimeric proteins Quantitative Immunoblotting, Co-IP, cell surface ELISA and interactome. Transient and stable expression of heterologous proteins and their characterization. Tissue culture proficiency of non-polarized and polarized cells. Confocal and light immunofluorescence microscopy, quantitative colocalization studies. Weekly progress report preparation, lab meeting attendance, and contributions to the smooth operation of the lab are expected. Position Summary: The Department of Physiology at McGill University is seeking a Research Assistant 1 to join an interdisciplinary research program. We study PMCA1, basigin, CFTR and other membrane protein structure-traffic relationship, interactions, and signaling using biochemical, morphological and biophysical assays . This is a Casual position with the possibility of renewal. Qualifications: Committed candidate must hold B.Sc. degree and have experience in biochemistry, and molecular and cell biology, fluorescence microscopy. Experience and strong background in the related fields. The Research Assistant 1 must have excellent organizational and communication skills and willing to participate in communal lab duties to facilitate the uninterrupted daily operation of the lab. Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. McGill University is an English-language university where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $30.54 Hours per Week: 34 (Part time) Location: McIntyre Medical Supervisor: Professor Position Start Date: 2026-09-21 Position End Date: 2026-12-31 Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-10 This position is covered by the Association of McGill University Research Employees (AMURE) collective agreement. McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/MacdonaldStewart-Bld/Cleaner--Mac-Powerhouse-_JR0000079659": {
      "title": "Cleaner (Mac Powerhouse)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: McGill University – Facilities Management and Ancillary Services - Macdonald Campus Position Summary: Under general supervision the incumbent ensures that the area to which he/she has been assigned is fully functional, clean, secure and in good operational order. Qualifications: English and French functional spoken and read. English or French functional written. Additional Details: Status: Full-Time Hours of Work: 38.75 hrs/week; Monday to Friday from 7:30 am to 3:45 pm. This position is located at the Macdonald Campus in Sainte-Anne-de-Bellevue As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 3 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Hourly Salary: $27.01 Hours per Week: 38.75 (Full time) Location: MacdonaldStewart Bld Supervisor: Custodial Supervisor (ER) Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-10 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
